        "note": "自我介绍的新信息落在名字 Paul 上。"
      },
      "I watch a film almost every evening, and my wife claims I am addicted.": {
        "primary": [
          "evening",
          "addicted"
        ],
        "secondary": [
          "almost"
        ],
        "rise": [],
        "fall": [],
        "note": "前半是几乎每晚都看，后半落在妻子说他上瘾，addicted 是判断焦点。"
      },
      "I would describe it differently: I am interested in narrative, and the cinema is where narrative is currently being rebuilt.": {
        "primary": [
          "differently",
          "narrative",
          "rebuilt"
        ],
        "secondary": [
          "cinema"
        ],
        "rise": [],
        "fall": [],
        "note": "他不同意「上瘾」的说法：真正兴趣在叙事，而电影正在重建叙事。"
      },
      "The most interesting writing in the last ten years has not been in films at all but in television, because a series can develop a character over eight hours instead of ninety minutes.": {
        "primary": [
          "television",
          "character"
        ],
        "secondary": [
          "films",
          "hours",
          "minutes"
        ],
        "rise": [],
        "fall": [],
        "note": "对比焦点是不在电影而在电视，因为剧集能用八小时而非九十分钟塑造角色。"
      },
      "However, the format also produces a lot of padding, and many series could be reduced by half without losing anything.": {
        "primary": [
          "padding",
          "half"
        ],
        "secondary": [
          "anything"
        ],
        "rise": [],
        "fall": [],
        "note": "两个分句各一核心：大量注水，以及砍掉一半也不损失内容。"
      },
      "Sequels and spin-offs are usually the weakest part of that economy: they are commissioned because the first instalment was profitable, not because anybody had a second story to tell.": {
        "primary": [
          "weakest",
          "profitable",
          "story"
        ],
        "secondary": [
          "Sequels",
          "spin-offs",
          "instalment"
        ],
        "rise": [],
        "fall": [],
        "note": "续集最弱，因为只是首部赚钱，而不是有人还有第二个故事要讲。"
      },
      "What irritates me is that predictability is punished as if it were a crime.": {
        "primary": [
          "irritates",
          "crime"
        ],
        "secondary": [
          "predictability"
        ],
        "rise": [],
        "fall": [],
        "note": "让他不满的是可预测性被当成罪过，crime 是比喻的落点。"
      },
      "Some of the best films I have seen were entirely predictable, and a cliché can still work if it is performed with conviction.": {
        "primary": [
          "predictable",
          "conviction"
